export default {"heading":"Life, work and legacy","introduction":"From university teaching to public administration, policy research and institution building: explore the life and contributions of ICUE’s founder in eight chapters.","readerHint":"Open any chapter, or read in order with Continue.","back":"Back","next":"Continue","complete":"Finish reading","completed":"Reading complete","counter":"Chapter {current} of {total}","sourceHref":"https://nguoidothi.net.vn/nghi-ve-mot-nguoi-cong-hien-21097.html","source":"A remembrance · 30.11.2019","photoEvents":{"2017":"VTV1 television interview","2018":"Meeting with his editorial colleagues"},"chapters":[{"id":"life","title":"Life and origins","period":"1931–2018","heading":"A life connected to Vietnam’s urban development","paragraphs":["Dr. Phạm Sỹ Liêm was born in 1931 in Diễn Thành, Diễn Châu, Nghệ An. A civil engineer, scholar and public administrator, he worked across university teaching, senior government service, scientific research and the creation of professional institutions.","His work repeatedly returned to the foundations of urban life: housing, land, public infrastructure, planning and governance. Across these different roles, he examined how professional knowledge and institutional reform could contribute to development.","He died on 30 November 2018, aged 87, or 88 by traditional Vietnamese age reckoning. His legacy connects engineering education, public service, independent policy research and organizations that continued beyond his lifetime, including ICUE."],"photoEvents":[]},{"id":"education","title":"Engineering education","period":"1958–1963","heading":"Helping establish reinforced-concrete engineering education","paragraphs":["During the 1950s and 1960s, he taught civil engineering and helped establish reinforced-concrete engineering education at Hanoi University of Science and Technology. The university’s construction faculty records identify his role in introducing the subject in the 1958–1959 academic year.","In October 1959, he was appointed the first head of the Reinforced Concrete Department. This was an early milestone in a career that involved developing both teaching and academic institutions.","He began postgraduate study in the Soviet Union in 1963 and subsequently continued his academic leadership. His experience in engineering education and research formed part of the foundation for his later public administration and urban policy work."],"photoEvents":[]},{"id":"public-service","title":"Public service and professional institutions","period":"From 1982","heading":"Government leadership and a stronger professional community","paragraphs":["His government career included service as Deputy Minister of Construction and Vice Chairman of the Hanoi People’s Committee. These roles brought his engineering background into contact with the practical administration of construction, infrastructure and urban development.","From 1982, he served as founding president of the Vietnam Federation of Civil Engineering Associations, leading its first three terms and later continuing as vice president.","His contribution extended beyond holding office. Over decades, he helped develop the federation’s organizational structure, research activities and professional influence. Building durable professional institutions was one of the important achievements remembered by his colleagues."],"photoEvents":[]},{"id":"institutes","title":"Building research institutes","period":"1999 · 2013","heading":"Two institutions for urban research and policy advice","paragraphs":["During the 1990s and 2000s, he expanded his research into urban governance, infrastructure and construction policy. In 1999, he founded the Institute for Urban Research and Infrastructure Development, providing an institutional base for work in these fields.","In 2013, he founded ICUE and became its inaugural director. This continued his work of creating organizations that connected research with policy advice and the practical challenges of development.","The two institutes reflect his sustained attention to urban planning, construction economics and infrastructure. For ICUE, his founding legacy lies in the combination of engineering knowledge, public administration experience and independent inquiry."],"photoEvents":[]},{"id":"policy","title":"Urban policy and public debate","period":"2012–2017","heading":"Specific contributions on land, planning and institutions","paragraphs":["Through books, research projects, conferences and interviews, he examined housing, land management, public infrastructure and urban governance. His work included public criticism of weaknesses in planning and policy implementation, making professional debate part of his contribution.","In 2012, he submitted detailed criticism of the draft Land Law through VCCI. His comments addressed land acquisition, property rights and transparency, showing his concern with how institutional rules affected both development and everyday life.","In 2016–2017, he took part in public discussions of the Planning Law, arguing for more coordinated national planning and stronger institutional reform. These contributions are recorded in policy submissions as well as recalled in professional memorials.","In 2017, he appeared in a VTV1 television interview. The archive photograph below records that interview."],"photoEvents":["2017"]},{"id":"editorial","title":"Người Đô Thị and editorial work","period":"2006–2018","heading":"A forum for urban affairs and quality of life","paragraphs":["In 2006, he co-founded Người Đô Thị, a magazine dedicated to urban affairs, and chaired its professional advisory board.","The publication became a platform for discussion of urban policy and quality of life. His work with the magazine added a public forum to his research and professional activities, bringing specialist questions into a wider conversation about cities.","He remained professionally involved with the magazine until his death. The 2018 photograph shows him meeting with his editorial colleagues at one of his final documented editorial meetings."],"photoEvents":["2018"]},{"id":"scholarship","title":"Scholarship into his final year","period":"September 2018","heading":"New Institutional Economics, published at the age of 87","paragraphs":["In 2017–2018, despite his advanced age, he continued researching and advising professional organizations. His academic curiosity remained active long after he had held senior government positions.","In September 2018, he published Tân kinh tế học thể chế (New Institutional Economics), his final major academic work. The book explored the relationship between institutions and economic development, continuing his longstanding interest in governance and reform.","Published when he was 87, it reportedly drew on more than 200 foreign references alongside Vietnamese research and policy documents. It stands as a record of sustained learning and intellectual work in the final year of his life."],"photoEvents":[]},{"id":"legacy","title":"The person remembered by colleagues","period":"Recollections at a 2019 memorial","heading":"Integrity, intellectual depth and a remarkable capacity for work","paragraphs":["Colleagues remembered a scholar who continued learning after reaching senior public office. Accounts of his life report that he spoke four foreign languages: English, French, Russian and Chinese.","At a 2019 memorial event, federation chairman Trần Ngọc Hùng recalled that, when travelling abroad, Dr. Liêm would seek out bookshops. He maintained an extensive personal library, read widely and even enjoyed martial-arts fiction.","Academician Phạm Hồng Giang described his legacy through three qualities: personal integrity, intellectual depth and an exceptional capacity for work. These are colleagues’ assessments and recollections, offering a view of the person behind the official posts and published work.","The 2019 article Nghĩ về một người cống hiến provides a more personal account through recollections by someone who worked with him for decades. For ICUE, his enduring legacy brings together engineering education, government service, independent inquiry, institution building and lifelong scholarship."],"photoEvents":[]}],"nguoiDoThi":"https://nguoidothi.net.vn/","remembrance":"https://nguoidothi.net.vn/nghi-ve-mot-nguoi-cong-hien-21097.html"}
